## PHASE 4 — Nginx reverse proxy (now that the app is actually running)

### Step 20. Create the Nginx site config
```
nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/lovecruz
```

Paste the following, adjusting domains/ports to match your actual services:

```nginx
server {
    server_name api.lovecruz.fun;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }
}

server {
    server_name media.lovecruz.fun;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:4000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }
}

server {
    server_name radio.lovecruz.fun;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:8000;
    }
}
```

Save and exit (`Ctrl + O`, `Enter`, `Ctrl + X`).

This tells Nginx:
- `api.lovecruz.fun` → Node API on port 3000
- `media.lovecruz.fun` → Mediasoup/media service on port 4000
- `radio.lovecruz.fun` → radio service on port 8000

### Step 21. Enable the site
```
ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/lovecruz /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
```

### Step 22. Test the config
```
nginx -t
```

### Step 23. Restart Nginx if the test passed
```
systemctl restart nginx
```

At this point, confirm DNS has actually propagated:
```
ping api.lovecruz.fun
```
(Ctrl+C to stop). It should resolve to your VPS IP. If it doesn't yet, wait before moving to SSL.

