## PHASE 5 — SSL with Let's Encrypt

### Step 24. Install Certbot
```
apt install certbot python3-certbot-nginx -y
```

### Step 25. Request certificates
```
certbot --nginx
```

Certbot will detect your Nginx config and prompt you to choose which domains to secure, e.g.:
```
lovecruz.fun
api.lovecruz.fun
media.lovecruz.fun
radio.lovecruz.fun
```

It will automatically obtain certificates, configure HTTPS, offer to redirect HTTP → HTTPS, and set up auto-renewal.

### Step 26. Verify auto-renewal works
```
certbot renew --dry-run
```

---

## PHASE 6 — Firewall (UFW)

### Step 27. Allow required ports
```
ufw allow OpenSSH
ufw allow 80
ufw allow 443
ufw allow 3478
ufw allow 5349
ufw allow 3000
ufw allow 4000
```

### Step 28. Open the Mediasoup UDP port range
```
ufw allow 40000:49999/udp
```

### Step 29. Enable the firewall
```
ufw enable
```

Confirm with:
```
ufw status
```

---

## PHASE 7 — Final checks

### Step 30. Confirm backend is alive
```
pm2 status
curl http://localhost:3000
```

### Step 31. Confirm Nginx is proxying correctly
```
curl -I https://api.lovecruz.fun
```

### Step 32. Confirm Postgres/Redis are running
```
systemctl status postgresql
systemctl status redis-server
```

### Step 33. Confirm the app can actually reach Postgres
```
sudo -u postgres psql -d lovecruz -c "\dt"
```
This should list your app's tables (the same ones your `db.js` startup test queries via `information_schema.tables`).

### Step 34. Test from a browser
Visit:
- `https://lovecruz.fun`
- `https://api.lovecruz.fun`
- `https://media.lovecruz.fun`
- `https://radio.lovecruz.fun`

All should load over HTTPS with a valid certificate (padlock icon, no warnings).

